  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MWI101299 Protection of Children from the Worst Forms of Child Labour in Sub-Saharan Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In view of this context and the issues at stake, the European Union, through DG INTPA, entrusted the NGO alliance Joining Forces (JFA) with the task of designing a new Action in 4 Sub-Saharan African countries (Mali, Burkina Faso, Madagascar, and Malawi) in order to &quot;Contribute to the reduction of child labor targeting its worst forms in Burkina Faso, Madagascar, Mali, and Malawi in line with the Sustainable Development Goals by 2025 - Target 8.7. This decision was made based on the positive experience of collaboration between the Joining Forces Alliance (JFA) and DG INTPA in the framework of an ongoing project in 5 Sub-Saharan African countries, as well as the field experience of its members in this area. _x000d_
_x000d_
The 6 NGO members of this JFA alliance decided to give the role of lead applicant for this project to World Vision Germany, in order to elaborate this Action with the other NGO members; in particular: &quot;Terre des Hommes&quot;, &quot;SOS Children&apos;s Village&quot;, &quot;Save the Children International&quot;, &quot;World Vision International&quot;, &quot;Plan International&quot; and &quot;Educo Spain&quot;. In each of the four countries targeted by the action, the NGOs were selected on the basis of their experience, cooperation and support to the local civil society, expertise and effective presence in the country, in order to ensure a quality implementation of the proposed action. Priority has also been given to affiliates of these NGOs to ensure the local anchoring of the Action (SOS Children&apos;s Village Burkina Faso). These NGOs will also guarantee a community anchoring in the areas most affected by child labor, especially its worst forms, accompanied by a comprehensive analysis of the issues, an interaction with the institutional level and an advocacy and learning strategy at the national and international level, thanks to their reputation and the support of JFA._x000d_
_x000d_
This Action will focus on 3 specific objectives: _x000d_
 _x000d_
&#x2022;	SO.1: The protection and action capacities of children, families and targeted communities as well as knowledge of their rights are increased, with particular attention to possible socio-economic alternatives to WFCL._x000d_
&#x2022;	SO.2: The capacities of local and national mechanisms and systems are strengthened to ensure the care of targeted girls/boys and the establishment of alternatives to WFCL_x000d_
&#x2022;	SO.3: Actions undertaken by state and non-state actors to prevent and reduce WFCL are supported in each country for better coordination, efficiency, visibility and transparency_x000d_
_x000d_
The interventions will be implemented in Lilongwe district.</narrative>
  </description>
